/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 342 0 R
/E (Training on the original buggy CIC-IDS2017 CSVs produces results that appear valid but rest on corrupted feature measurements. Among corrected-dataset approaches, our result sits within half a point of the benchmark paper's RF baseline, despite deliberately using the harder labeling convention and evaluating on full, unfiltered class sizes. Reporting that the naive fusion was worse than XGBoost alone is itself a methodological contribution.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [7]
